35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The roads closed, but the halls stayed open. That is a good sign for us.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The digitisation project failed, but the evening groups survived. That is a useful distinction.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"I found a gap. We have volunteers, but no one to manage them properly.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The grant is a trap. It pays for a year, then we are on our own.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The bus links are gone. The outer wards are cut off from us.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, if the grant ends, do we have a fallback?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,The evening groups prove that community-led models work without our direct funding.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,We cannot hire new staff. We must use what is already in the room.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,The equipment money was wasted on things we did not need. The running costs are real.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I am worried. If the buses stop, who comes to the library?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I think we should focus on the evening room bookings. They seem resilient.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. The remote catalogue use is also strong. It bypasses the road issues.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,I object to hiring. I propose we leverage the existing volunteer network for supervision.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree with Shion. We must not add fixed costs. We need flexible, low-cost options.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"The remote catalogue helps, but it does not replace the human touch for those who are isolated.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"So, we are looking at evening rooms and remote access?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Yes. The data supports it. The evening groups and remote use are the stable points.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I will support that, provided we do not promise new staff. We use the volunteers.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,That aligns with the budget reality. No new fixed lines. Just flexible use of existing assets.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am relieved. It feels less like a burden and more like a support.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
